.IX Title "Mouse::Exporter 3pm"
.TH Mouse::Exporter 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Mouse::Exporter \- make an import() and unimport() just like Mouse.pm
.SH VERSION
.IX Header "VERSION"
This document describes Mouse version v2.6.2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    package MyApp::Mouse;
\&
\&    use Mouse ();
\&    use Mouse::Exporter;
\&
\&    Mouse::Exporter\->setup_import_methods(
\&      as_is => [ \*(Aqhas_rw\*(Aq, \*(Aqother_sugar\*(Aq, \e&Some::Random::thing ],
\&      also  => \*(AqMouse\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&
\&    sub has_rw {
\&        my $meta = caller\->meta;
\&        my ( $name, %options ) = @_;
\&        $meta\->add_attribute(
\&          $name,
\&          is => \*(Aqrw\*(Aq,
\&          %options,
\&        );
\&    }
\&
\&    # then later ...
\&    package MyApp::User;
\&
\&    use MyApp::Mouse;
\&
\&    has \*(Aqname\*(Aq;
\&    has_rw \*(Aqsize\*(Aq;
\&    thing;
\&
\&    no MyApp::Mouse;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This module encapsulates the exporting of sugar functions in a
\&\f(CW\*(C`Mouse.pm\*(C'\fR\-like manner. It does this by building custom \f(CW\*(C`import\*(C'\fR,
\&\f(CW\*(C`unimport\*(C'\fR methods for your module, based on a spec you provide.
.PP
Note that \f(CW\*(C`Mouse::Exporter\*(C'\fR does not provide the \f(CW\*(C`with_meta\*(C'\fR option,
but you can easily get the metaclass by \f(CW\*(C`caller\->meta\*(C'\fR as "SYNOPSIS" shows.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.ie n .SS "setup_import_methods( ARGS )"
.el .SS "\f(CWsetup_import_methods( ARGS )\fP"
.IX Subsection "setup_import_methods( ARGS )"
.ie n .SS """build_import_methods( ARGS ) \-> (\e&import, \e&unimport)"""
.el .SS "\f(CWbuild_import_methods( ARGS ) \-> (\e&import, \e&unimport)\fP"
.IX Subsection "build_import_methods( ARGS ) -> (&import, &unimport)"
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
Moose::Exporter
